{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793643346213553511,"compiled_state":{"alias":"typical-endurant-boubou","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"2354f648b22d592d31af29cba894f877c05ff947c163dc11e03a8e0754e8e142","event_uuid":"24738308-16f4-4e03-a563-7a5604823b8c","position":{"commit_sha":"cd1be3d5a7f61f51e885284c8e1b3284e1d0d869","position":"1793640917197601386-24738308-16f4-4e03-a563-7a5604823b8c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1b196f6658580ab329a25187d8f407becf16e0b23127af1f5865f42ac63ab30f","event_uuid":"ae1a204b-5167-4db5-88d0-6cb7306e5d49","position":{"commit_sha":"0840af3cbebc4c54d9f8413907b12a1cdb5c5129","position":"1793641078992992620-ae1a204b-5167-4db5-88d0-6cb7306e5d49"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ec1e8f6741bc3cad537fda2bb0cd1a4bb7cc256dbed40b63b72f93a818a3c6a6","event_uuid":"64dfaaf7-61e9-44a8-91ea-52c8fba82e0a","position":{"commit_sha":"8a4ed322f98921b66149b04a4be1967655e34ed0","position":"1793641091254648921-64dfaaf7-61e9-44a8-91ea-52c8fba82e0a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"abbf4787574f662f0849a46d52b777853bb75cd04bc7f9abd78fa6280e8ff5ab","event_uuid":"c175bc8c-4d8b-45a4-9455-bd418ea4d4e2","position":{"commit_sha":"dba26710c650f3cc6759061bcfd7177e198fda35","position":"1793641091256289561-c175bc8c-4d8b-45a4-9455-bd418ea4d4e2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Prior art, and why this is a follow-on rather than a duplicate\n\nTwo closed tickets cover adjacent ground. Neither closes this gap.\n\n**`fd6b-09c5-8f76-45ad`** (\"docs/exit-codes.md has drifted from ROUTES and advertises a\ngate it lacks\", mirror F12) is the ticket that ADDED the parity test. Before it, the only\nassertion touching the file was `assert \"\\`11\\`\" in text and \"block-but-retryable\" in\ntext.lower()` -- nothing checked the table at all. fd6b fixed that and narrowed the\nfile's claim on the **exit-value** axis (`:12-15`: \"those columns are hand-authored\").\nIt did not qualify the claim on the **nesting** axis, which is what this bug reports.\n\n**`f0ff-028a-f5cb-4b66`** (\"Make docs/exit-codes.md complete and keep it that way\") is the\nsharper one. It closed with this acceptance criterion ticked:\n\n> - [x] A CI check asserts every dispatcher arm has a row, so a new command without one\n>       fails\n\nThat criterion is **not satisfied as written**, and this ticket is the demonstration.\n`rebar store build-vectors` is a new dispatcher arm. It shipped with no row. `make verify`\npassed twice. The omission was caught by an LLM code-review advisory on Gerrit change\n3218, not by CI.\n\nThe criterion is satisfied only under a reading of \"dispatcher arm\" that means top-level\nroute, which is not how the surrounding description uses it -- f0ff's own description\ncounts \"75 real commands ... from `_cli/_help.known_subcommands()` union\n`_cli/__init__._INTERCEPTS`\", a set that necessarily includes nested members, against\n`_live_route_names()`'s 53.\n\nSo the enforcement gap is not a regression since f0ff; it is the gap f0ff believed it had\nclosed. That makes the documentation route (narrow the claim) and the enforcement route\n(make the claim true) a genuine choice rather than a formality, and it is why this ticket\noffers both and requires the chosen one to be demonstrated by mutation rather than\nasserted. f0ff's AC was ticked without such a demonstration, which is how it came to be\nwrong.","timestamp":1793641078992992620}],"created_at":1793640917197601386,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"64dfaaf7-61e9-44a8-91ea-52c8fba82e0a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0461-09ce-4850-42a7"},{"link_uuid":"c175bc8c-4d8b-45a4-9455-bd418ea4d4e2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f0ff-028a-f5cb-4b66"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`docs/exit-codes.md` declares itself (`:5-6`) \"the single source of truth for ... which\ncode each subcommand emits\", and states (`:7-15`) that\n`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py` \"cross-checks this file's per-command\ntable against the route registry, so a route with no row here ... fails the build.\"\n\nThat guarantee holds only for **top-level** routes. It does not hold for nested\nsubcommands, which is where most of the table's rows live.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`_live_route_names()` (`test_exit_codes.py:247-249`) builds\n`{route.name for route in ROUTES if not route.retired}`. Measured on the live registry:\n\n    'store' in live          -> True\n    'store build-vectors'... -> 'build-vectors' in live -> False\n    'footprint' in live      -> False\n    len(live)                -> 53\n\nThe parity test's own docstring (`:254`) is accurate and says so plainly: \"each table\nrow begins with a live top-level route. Nested invocations share that route.\" The\n`orphaned` check keys on `row.split()[0]`, so a row for any `store <member>` is\naccepted because `store` is live, and the `undocumented` check can never demand a row\nfor a member because no member name is in `live`.\n\nNet effect: a new nested subcommand can land with no row, and nothing fails. Observed\ndirectly — `rebar store build-vectors` (ticket 0461-09ce-4850-42a7) passed `make verify`\ntwice with no row in the table. The gap was caught by an LLM code-review advisory, not\nby the build.\n\nThe table nonetheless carries a row for every other `store` member (`compact`, `fsck`,\n`fsck-recover`, `maintenance`, `footprint`, `doctor`, `export`, `import` at `:159-202`),\nso the convention is real and maintained by hand while the doc describes it as enforced.\n\n## Why this matters beyond one missing row\n\nThis is the same defect class the file already documents about itself at `:12-15`:\n\"Until 2026-09 this file claimed a stronger guarantee than any test made, and the table\nhad drifted in both directions while carrying that claim.\" That correction narrowed the\nclaim on the *exit-value* axis (those columns are hand-authored) but left the\n*row-coverage* claim unqualified, and on the nesting axis it is still too strong.\n\nA doc that overstates its own enforcement is worse than one that states none: a reader\nwho trusts `:7-15` has no reason to check the table by hand, which is exactly how the\n`build-vectors` row came to be missing.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/exit-codes.md` no longer claims a guarantee the parity test does not make:\n      the row-coverage sentence states that enforcement covers top-level routes and\n      that nested-subcommand rows are maintained by convention -- OR the parity test is\n      extended so the claim becomes true.\n- [ ] If the enforcement route is taken, a test fails when a live nested subcommand has\n      no row, demonstrated by a mutation (remove one existing member row; the test\n      must fail) and by the inverse (an invented member row names a real nested\n      invocation or the test fails).\n- [ ] If the documentation route is taken, the narrowed wording is shown to be accurate\n      against `_live_route_names()` as measured, not asserted.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe missing `store build-vectors` row itself -- that is fixed in 0461-09ce-4850-42a7's\nown change, which is where the omission arose.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","f0ff-028a-f5cb-4b66"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","docs"],"ticket_id":"e095-4b4e-de40-4fd2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"exit-codes.md claims a route-row guarantee the parity test does not make for nested subcommands","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["24738308-16f4-4e03-a563-7a5604823b8c","ae1a204b-5167-4db5-88d0-6cb7306e5d49","64dfaaf7-61e9-44a8-91ea-52c8fba82e0a","c175bc8c-4d8b-45a4-9455-bd418ea4d4e2"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793643346213553511,"uuid":"23633386-44a6-4461-b8db-20d89ed7f415"}